media information, otherwise ignore cbtables data.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: Ia4a8848fd7db9d9a2bf9f5c226566fe3936ff543 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308520 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308520" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/20/308520/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ic2de49e53079e6d5e6a554435cb996a2173fcb39" commit="642f0b1499c7050914ae7b89b833db01ddb93561" commit_message="UPSTREAM: cbfstool: Add bintohex function  We need to emit some hex strings.  Change-Id: Ic2de49e53079e6d5e6a554435cb996a2173fcb39 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Commit-Id: ca97fa7ac3c035532bbf493613c644514313a190 Original-Change-Id: I9e7e184282f6ad0470f2e269f5dc874e78f8b697 Original-Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;patrick@georgi-clan.de&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11766 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308781 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308781" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/81/308781/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I93e9ef8b1d2392a1532160f8669617bb6d029833" commit="2f65ac71015a30ab694cff9398e0273d49d97ebd" commit_message="UPSTREAM: cbfstool: prefer fmap data over cbfs master header if it exists  Up to now, if both fmap and a master header existed, the master header was used. Now, use the master header only if no fmap is found.  Change-Id: I93e9ef8b1d2392a1532160f8669617bb6d029833 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Commit-Id: 2f953d304e02be9a2f4f6fbd86b41dd6c86ec5db Original-Change-Id: Iafbf2c9dc325597e23a9780b495549b5d912e9ad Original-Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11629 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308782 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308782" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/82/308782/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaa5f41f0874a9da8d7b4db9c3f7126d69e85c65b" commit="6734a23e04df35eb61e9e361cb9ec040ce3e74c7" commit_message="sys-apps/coreboot-utils: import vboot_platform  We use that in cbfstool now for adding hashes to CBFS files.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=tot TEST=none  Change-Id: Iaa5f41f0874a9da8d7b4db9c3f7126d69e85c65b Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309340 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309340" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/40/309340/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="If01c068581bcb75648d5c195c4a06cc4dbfbd5a0" commit="ec5967b07e30a4af5aa4a29522816397b49477f9" commit_message="UPSTREAM: cbfstool: Add support for hashes as file metadata  They allow optimizing a verification of a whole CBFS image by only dealing with the headers (assuming you choose to trust the hash algorithm(s)).  The format allows for multiple hashes for a single file, and cbfstool can handle them, but right now it can't generate such headers.  Loosely based on Sol's work in http://review.coreboot.org/#/c/10147/, but using the compatible file attribute format. vboot is now a hard dependency of the build process, but we import it into the tree for quite a while now.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=tot TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:309340  Change-Id: If01c068581bcb75648d5c195c4a06cc4dbfbd5a0 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Commit-Id: 89f20340d5a4c14ab76d3612cd33fff8894602ec Original-Change-Id: I9f14f30537d676ce209ad612e7327c6f4810b313 Original-Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;patrick@georgi-clan.de&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11767 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308783 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308783" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/83/308783/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0b0bec24a11b8fa7e39ab1218fa5d027487e57c3" commit="11ba7db8932df7c47cf465abb4ce3422a10ed17f" commit_message="overlord: FixtureWindow: use jQuery.html instead of dom.innerText  Firefox does not support dom.innerText. Use jQuery.html for better portability.  BUG=chromium:443972 TEST=manually  Change-Id: I0b0bec24a11b8fa7e39ab1218fa5d027487e57c3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309267 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309267" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/67/309267/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib8c8ca7d9fb062aa485b79e45bb1be4abafcceba" commit="ebf42a3024944f8feccf415945c0c36b5ded481f" commit_message="overlord: TerminalWindow: replace onClose with onCloseClicked  We should bind to the onCloseClicked handler instead of the onClose hanlder so we can close terminal window for websockets that are not connected.  BUG=none TEST=manually  Change-Id: Ib8c8ca7d9fb062aa485b79e45bb1be4abafcceba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309353 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309353" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/53/309353/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I524e7eb5674f2061791cca920c8e1b4c35805d3c" commit="791f7cb6eabd4637bba699e88d9b86fcfeb03151" commit_message="vboot: ec: Check for EC limit power request in VbExEcVbootDone()  Add VbExEcVbootDone(), which checks the limit power flag that gets set by the EC to request that the AP limit its power use. If this flag remains set for 3 seconds, request a system shutdown since we're likely to brownout if we continue to boot.  BUG=chromium:537269 TEST=Manual on Glados. Set CHG_MW thresh to 20000, BAT_PCT to 50. Verify that LIMIT_POWER parameter is set until Zinger negotiates to 20V. Also verify that we do not proceed with boot when Donette is plugged. BRANCH=None  Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I524e7eb5674f2061791cca920c8e1b4c35805d3c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307885 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307885" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/85/307885/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0c0d662c42435481829cee42d26c70603a3c0935" commit="0a6fea67a62bf4cce141ed84931eda7838eb0d08" commit_message="CHROMIUM: HID: i2c-hid - Handle all pending reports and unstick touches on resume  In the case that the system was suspended or runtime suspend occurred while touches were being tracked, we would have stuck points on resume if the fingers left while the device was in low power state.  First, lets handle all pending reports from the device that may have been missed as interrupts were disabled on suspend.  Then, after the device has been hwreset, we call reset_resume. hid-multitouch has been modified to release all slots.  This change also removes the had_suspended flag, and always does the full hwreset and reset_resume on i2c_hid_runtime_resume, as these are now required to make sure that there isn't any stray reports from the device from before suspend, and to release stuck touches.  Signed-off-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46488 TEST=Enable Android's touch debugging options in Developer Options Place 5+ fingers on touchscreen while on. Turn off display with the power button. Remove fingers Turn on display with the power button. Check that the 5 points are not stuck on resume.  Change-Id: I0c0d662c42435481829cee42d26c70603a3c0935 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308554 Commit-Ready: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308554" owner_email="bleung@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/308554/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I45d4aa0f0d4280e68282ea11ccfda05201f88aae" commit="a8af572bc564303c127977b87d77b2845f4da1d9" commit_message="oak: ensure PMIC power button is released after SYSJUMP.  There is a race condition between SYSJUMP and function release_pmic_pwron_deferred(). Process of EC SW Sync will delay the execution time of release_pmic_pwron_deferred(). PMIC will shutdown the power, if PMIC power button can not be released within 8 seconds (depends on PMIC spec). In order to ensure PMIC power button will be released in time, just release it after SYSJUMP.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46392 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46656 BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall -j; Enable EC SW sync and normal mode in coreboot, Kernel should bootup successfully.  Change-Id: I45d4aa0f0d4280e68282ea11ccfda05201f88aae Signed-off-by: Ben Lok &lt;ben.lok@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307220 Reviewed-by: Rong Chang &lt;rongchang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307220" owner_email="ben.lok@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/20/307220/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7590.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>